The Attorney is authorised to do the following in the name of and on behalf of the Principal:
{{powers_granted}}
and, in connection with and only so far as is necessary for those acts:
(a) to sign, execute, and deliver any document, application, form, declaration, or acknowledgment;
(b) to appear before, and to make representations to, any public authority, office, court, or tribunal, and to sign and file any paper required by it;
(c) to receive and give valid receipts for any sum payable to the Principal;
(d) to correspond with any bank, authority, or person, and to obtain and give information;
(e) generally to do everything that is necessary and incidental to the acts expressly authorised above.
The authority in sub-clauses (a) to (e) is ancillary. It does not enlarge the acts expressly authorised, and shall be construed strictly by reference to them.
